# --- Data & model weights: never commit. Use the download/export scripts. ---
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
# Menu CSVs are versioned inputs, not downloaded artifacts: commit them.
!data/menu/
data/menu/fastfood_nutrition.csv
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# ...except the two files the inference service actually loads. Committing a
# 5MB model is a deliberate trade: reproducing it otherwise means a 46GB
# download, 72 minutes of MediaPipe, and a training run, which is too high a
# bar for a teammate who just wants to see the demo work after a clone.
#
# The cost is that every committed model stays in git history forever. So
# commit a model when it is worth keeping, not after every experiment. The
# .pt checkpoints stay ignored -- they are only needed to resume training.
!ml/asl/artifacts/sign_classifier.onnx
!ml/asl/artifacts/labels.json
*.gguf
*.tflite
*.safetensors
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/

